But if I have 500-some site, that's alot of typing (yes I could define all the generators within a loop).

Using a tip you wrote elsewhere, I did get this below to work; I guess this is an example of the alarm/beep dichotomy from the docs: I can either have an alarm (site) with a trajectory that generates beeps (patients), or I can have a beep (patient) trajectory.

N <- 100

site <- trajectory() %>%

  log_(function() paste0("site startup: ", as.character(now(env)))) %>%
  timeout(function () rexp(1, get_attribute(env, "rate"))) %>%
  log_(function() paste0("  patient enrolled ", as.character(now(env)))) %>%
  set_global("count", function() {
    count <- get_global(env, "count") + 1
    if (is.na <http://is.na>(count)) count <- 1
    count
  }) %>%
  rollback(amount = 3, check=function() { get_global(env, "count") <= N })

env %<>%
  add_dataframe("site",
                site,
                site_data) %>%
  run()

